xref:join_text[The result of joining ``text''^{asterisk}^`` with separator ``t~sep~``]

. If ``text''^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``""``.
. Else if let ``t~h~`` be ``text''^{asterisk}^``:
 .. Return ``t~h~``.
. Else if let ``t~h1~ {two-colons} text^{asterisk}^`` be ``text''^{asterisk}^``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``t~h2~ {two-colons} t~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``text^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Return ``t~h1~`` concatenated with ``t~sep~`` concatenated with xref:join_text[the result of joining ``t~h2~ {two-colons} t~t~^{asterisk}^`` with separator ``t~sep~``].

xref:replace_text[The text ``t`` with all occurrences of ``t~old~`` replaced by ``t~new~``]

. Return ``xref:replace_text'[$replace_text'(0, the length of t, t, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

xref:replace_text'[$replace_text'(n~len''~, n~len'''~, t, t~old~, t~new~)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is equal to ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Return ``t``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is less than ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Let ``t~replaced~`` be <<ite,``t`` with ``[n~len''~]`` set to ``t~new~`` if ``t[n~len''~]`` is equal to ``t~old~`` otherwise ``t``>>.
  ... Return ``xref:replace_text'[$replace_text'(n~len''~ + 1, n~len'''~, t~replaced~, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

xref:replace_text_except[The text ``t`` with all occurrences of ``t~old~`` not replaced by ``t~new~``]

. Return ``xref:replace_text_except'[$replace_text_except'(0, the length of t, t, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

xref:replace_text_except'[$replace_text_except'(n~len''~, n~len'''~, t, t~old~, t~new~)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is equal to ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Return ``t``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is less than ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Let ``t~replaced~`` be <<ite,``t`` if ``t[n~len''~]`` is equal to ``t~old~`` otherwise ``t`` with ``[n~len''~]`` set to ``t~new~``>>.
  ... Return ``xref:replace_text_except'[$replace_text_except'(n~len''~ + 1, n~len'''~, t~replaced~, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

