xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[``typeIR''`` can be default-initialized]

. If let ``boolTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``boolTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.
 return ``true``.
. Else if let ``errorTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``errorTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+ERROR+``.
 return ``true``.
. Else if let ``stringTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``stringTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+STRING+``.
 return ``true``.
. Else if let ``integerTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``true``.
. Else if let ``+TYPEDEF+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[``typeIR`` can be default-initialized].
. Else if let ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[``typeIR`` can be default-initialized].
. Else if let ``+TUPLE+ +<+typeIR^{asterisk}^+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:forall_[all ``$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^`` are true].
. Else if let ``typeIR +[+++_+++]+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[``typeIR`` can be default-initialized].
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR ++_++ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:forall_[all ``$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^`` are true].
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR ++_++ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:forall_[all ``$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^`` are true].
. Else if let ``+HEADER_UNION+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR ++_++ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:forall_[all ``$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^`` are true].
. Else if let ``+ENUM+ ++_++ +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``true``.
. Else if let ``+ENUM+ ++_++ +<+typeIR+>+ +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:is_defaultable_typeIR[``typeIR`` can be default-initialized].
. Return ``false``.

xref:is_equalable_typeIR[``typeIR''`` supports equality comparison]

. If let ``voidTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``voidTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+VOID+``.
 return ``false``.
. Else if let ``typeId`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``false``.
. Else if let ``+TYPEDEF+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:is_equalable_typeIR[``typeIR`` supports equality comparison].
. Else if let ``externObjectTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``false``.
. Else if let ``parserObjectTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``false``.
. Else if let ``controlObjectTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``false``.
. Else if let ``packageObjectTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``: return ``false``.
