 .. Let ``typeIR~unroll~`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR`` with typedefs unrolled].
 .. Return xref:cast_record[``recordValue`` casted to type ``typeIR~unroll~``].
. Else if let ``defaultValue`` be ``value``:
 .. Check that ``defaultValue`` matches pattern ``+DEFAULT+``.

 .. Let ``typeIR~unroll~`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR`` with typedefs unrolled].
 .. Return xref:cast_default[``+DEFAULT+`` casted to type ``typeIR~unroll~``].
. Else if let ``invalidHeaderValue`` be ``value``:
 .. Let ``typeIR~unroll~`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR`` with typedefs unrolled].
 .. Return xref:cast_invalid_header[``+{#}+`` casted to type ``typeIR~unroll~``].
. Else if let ``setValue`` be ``value``:
 .. Let ``typeIR~unroll~`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR`` with typedefs unrolled].
 .. Return xref:cast_set[``setValue`` casted to type ``typeIR~unroll~``].

xref:default[The default value for type ``typeIR''``]

. If let ``boolTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``boolTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

 .. Return ``false``.
. Else if let ``errorTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``errorTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+ERROR+``.

 .. Return ``+ERROR+ +.+ "NoError"``.
. Else if let ``stringTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``stringTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+STRING+``.

 .. Let ``text~empty~`` be ``""``.
 .. Return ``+"+ text~empty~ +"+``.
. Else if let ``intTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``intTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

 .. Return ``+D+ 0``.
. Else if let ``+BIT+ +<+w+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``w +W+ 0``.
. Else if let ``+INT+ +<+w+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``w +S+ 0``.
. Else if let ``+VARBIT+ +<+w+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``w +.+ 0 +V+ 0``.
. Else if let ``+TYPEDEF+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:default[the default value for type ``typeIR``].
. Else if let ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return xref:default[the default value for type ``typeIR``].
. Else if let ``+TUPLE+ +<+typeIR^{asterisk}^+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+TUPLE+ +(+xref:default[$default(typeIR)]^{asterisk}^+)+``.
. Else if let ``typeIR +[+n~s~+]+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let ``value^{asterisk}^`` be xref:repeat_[a list of ``n~s~`` copies of the default value for type ``typeIR``].
 .. Return ``+HEADER_STACK+ +[+value^{asterisk}^ +(+0 +;+ n~s~+)++]+``.
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+STRUCT+ typeId +{+( xref:default[$default(typeIR~f~)] id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+HEADER+ typeId +{+false +;+ ( xref:default[$default(typeIR~f~)] id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER_UNION+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~f~ id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Return ``+HEADER_UNION+ typeId +{+( xref:default[$default(typeIR~f~)] id~f~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``+ENUM+ typeId +{+id^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``id~f_h~ {two-colons} ++_++^{asterisk}^`` be ``id^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Return ``typeId +.+ id~f_h~``.
. Else if let ``+ENUM+ typeId +<+typeIR+>+ +{+( nameIR~field~ +=+ value~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let ``value~zero~`` be xref:cast_int[``+D+ 0`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
 .. Let ``id^?^`` be xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``value~zero~`` in ``( value~field~, nameIR~field~ )^{asterisk}^``].
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Let!~type~ ``id~zero~`` be ``id^?^``.

   .... Return ``typeId +.+ id~zero~ +.+ value~zero~``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``value~zero~`` in ``( value~field~, nameIR~field~ )^{asterisk}^``].

   .... Let ``id~zero~`` be ``"__UNSPECIFIED"``.
   .... Return ``typeId +.+ id~zero~ +.+ value~zero~``.

xref:cast_to_enum[``value`` casted to enum type ``enumTypeIR``]

. Let!~type~ ``+ENUM+ typeId +<+typeIR+>+ +{+valueFieldIR^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``enumTypeIR``.

. Return ``xref:cast_to_enum'[$cast_to_enum'(typeId, typeIR, valueFieldIR^{asterisk}^, value)]``.

xref:cast_to_enum'[$cast_to_enum'(typeId, typeIR, valueFieldIR^{asterisk}^, value~target~)]

. If ``valueFieldIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Let ``value~idx~`` be xref:cast_op[``value~target~`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
 .. Let ``id~unnamed~`` be ``"__UNSPECIFIED"``.
 .. Return ``typeId +.+ id~unnamed~ +.+ value~idx~``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``nameIR +=+ value +;+`` be ``valueFieldIR~h~``.
 .. If xref:bin_eq[``value`` ``+==+`` ``value~target~``]:
  ... Return ``typeId +.+ nameIR +.+ value``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``xref:cast_to_enum'[$cast_to_enum'(typeId, typeIR, valueFieldIR~t~^{asterisk}^, value~target~)]``.

xref:cast_bool[``boolValue'`` casted to type ``typeIR''``]

. Let ``b`` be ``boolValue'``.
. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``boolTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``.

  ... Check that ``boolTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

  ... Return ``b``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+BIT+ +<+w+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``boolValue'`` is equal to ``true``.

     ...... Return ``w +W+ 1``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``boolValue'`` is equal to ``false``.

     ...... Return ``w +W+ 0``.
  ... Else if let ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
   .... Return xref:cast_bool[``boolValue'`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
  ... Else if let ``+SET+ +<+typeIR+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
   .... Return ``+SET+ +{+xref:cast_bool[$cast_bool(typeIR, boolValue')]+}+``.

xref:cast_int[``integerValue`` casted to type ``typeIR''``]

. If let ``boolTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``boolTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+BOOL+``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return ``i =/= 0``.
 .. Else if let ``w +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return ``i =/= 0``.
. Else if let ``intTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``intTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+INT+``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return ``+D+ i``.
 .. Else if let ``++_++ +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return ``+D+ i``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``+D+ xref:bitstr_to_int[$bitstr_to_int(w, i)]``.
. Else if let ``+BIT+ +<+w~to~+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Let ``i~cast~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w~to~`` representing the integer ``i``].
  ... Return ``w~to~ +W+ i~cast~``.
 .. Else if let ``++_++ +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Let ``i~cast~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w~to~`` representing the integer ``i``].
  ... Return ``w~to~ +W+ i~cast~``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``i~from~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i`` of width ``w~from~``].
  ... Let ``i~cast~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w~to~`` representing the integer ``i~from~``].
  ... Return ``w~to~ +W+ i~cast~``.
. Else if let ``+INT+ +<+w~to~+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Let ``i~cast~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w~to~`` representing the integer ``i``].
  ... Return ``w~to~ +S+ i~cast~``.
 .. Else if let ``++_++ +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Let ``i~cast~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w~to~`` representing the integer ``i``].
  ... Return ``w~to~ +S+ i~cast~``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``i~from~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i`` of width ``w~from~``].
  ... Let ``i~cast~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w~to~`` representing the integer ``i~from~``].
  ... Return ``w~to~ +S+ i~cast~``.
. Else if let ``+VARBIT+ +<+w~max~+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``w~max'~ +.+ w +V+ i`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. Check that ``w~max~`` is equal to ``w~max'~``.

 .. Return ``w~max~ +.+ w +V+ i``.
. Else if let ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return xref:cast_op[``+D+ i`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
 .. Else if let ``w +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return xref:cast_op[``w +W+ i`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
 .. Else:
  ... Return xref:cast_op[``w +S+ i`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
. Else if let ``enumTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. If let ``w +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return xref:cast_to_enum[``w +W+ i`` casted to enum type ``enumTypeIR``].
 .. Else if let ``w +S+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return xref:cast_to_enum[``w +S+ i`` casted to enum type ``enumTypeIR``].
. Else if let ``+SET+ +<+typeIR+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``integerValue``.

 .. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return ``+SET+ +{+xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, +D+ i)]+}+``.
 .. Else if let ``w +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
  ... Return ``+SET+ +{+xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, w +W+ i)]+}+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``+SET+ +{+xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, w +S+ i)]+}+``.

xref:cast_error[``errorValue'`` casted to type ``typeIR''``]

. Let ``+ERROR+ +.+ nameIR`` be ``errorValue'``.
. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``errorTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``.

  ... Check that ``errorTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+ERROR+``.

  ... Return ``+ERROR+ +.+ nameIR``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+SET+ +<+typeIR+>+`` be ``typeIR''``.

  ... Return ``+SET+ +{+xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, errorValue')]+}+``.

<<cast_list,``+LIST+ +[+value^{asterisk}^+]+`` casted to type ``typeIR'``>>

. Let!~type~ ``+LIST+ +<+typeIR+>+`` be ``typeIR'``.

. Return ``+LIST+ +[+( xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, value)] )^{asterisk}^+]+``.

<<cast_header_stack,``+HEADER_STACK+ +[+value^{asterisk}^ +(+n~idx~ +;+ n~size'~+)++]+`` casted to type ``typeIR'``>>

. Let!~type~ ``typeIR +[+n~size~+]+`` be ``typeIR'``.

. Check that ``n~size~`` is equal to ``n~size'~``.

. Return ``+HEADER_STACK+ +[+value^{asterisk}^ +(+n~idx~ +;+ n~size~+)++]+``.

xref:cast_struct[``+STRUCT+ typeId' +{+( value~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` casted to type ``typeIR``]

. Let!~type~ ``+STRUCT+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR``.

. Check that ``typeId`` is equal to ``typeId'``.

. Return ``+STRUCT+ typeId +{+( value~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.

xref:cast_header[``+HEADER+ typeId' +{+b +;+ ( value~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` casted to type ``typeIR``]

. Let!~type~ ``+HEADER+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR``.

. Check that ``typeId`` is equal to ``typeId'``.

. Return ``+HEADER+ typeId +{+b +;+ ( value~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.

xref:cast_enum[``enumValue`` casted to type ``typeIR''``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``+ENUM+ typeId +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``typeId' +.+ nameIR`` be ``enumValue``.

   .... Check that ``typeId`` is equal to ``typeId'``.

   .... Return ``typeId +.+ nameIR``.
  ... Else if let ``+ENUM+ typeId +<+++_+++>+ +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``typeId' +.+ nameIR +.+ value`` be ``enumValue``.

   .... Check that ``typeId`` is equal to ``typeId'``.

   .... Return ``typeId +.+ nameIR +.+ value``.
  ... Else if let ``+SET+ +<+typeIR+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
   .... Return ``+SET+ +{+xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, enumValue)]+}+``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``++_++ +.+ ++_++ +.+ value`` be ``enumValue``.

  ... Check that ``typeIR''`` does not have type ``serializableEnumTypeIR`` and ``typeIR''`` does not have type ``setTypeIR``.

  ... Return xref:cast_op[``value`` casted to type ``typeIR''``].

xref:cast_sequence[``sequenceValue`` casted to type ``typeIR''``]

. If let ``+LIST+ +<+typeIR+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``sequenceValue``.

 .. Return ``+LIST+ +[+( xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, value)] )^{asterisk}^+]+``.
. Else if let ``+TUPLE+ +<+typeIR^{asterisk}^+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``sequenceValue``.

 .. Return ``+TUPLE+ +(+( xref:cast_op[$cast_op(typeIR, value)] )^{asterisk}^+)+``.
. Else if let ``typeIR +[+n~size~+]+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``sequenceValue``.

 .. Let ``value~cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value`` casted to type ``typeIR``], for all ``value`` in ``value^{asterisk}^`` and ``value~cast~`` in ``value~cast~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let ``n~idx~`` be the length of ``value^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Return ``+HEADER_STACK+ +[+value~cast~^{asterisk}^ +(+n~idx~ +;+ n~size~+)++]+``.
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``sequenceValue``.

 .. Let ``value~cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value`` casted to type ``typeIR~field~``], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``, ``value`` in ``value^{asterisk}^``, and ``value~cast~`` in ``value~cast~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Return ``+STRUCT+ typeId +{+( value~cast~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``sequenceValue``.

 .. Let ``value~cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value`` casted to type ``typeIR~field~``], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``, ``value`` in ``value^{asterisk}^``, and ``value~cast~`` in ``value~cast~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Return ``+HEADER+ typeId +{+true +;+ ( value~cast~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.

xref:cast_record[``recordValue`` casted to type ``typeIR``]

. If let ``+STRUCT+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~t_field~ id~t_field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+RECORD+ +{+( value~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``recordValue``.

 .. Let ``value^?^`` be xref:find_map[the value of ``id~t_field~`` in map ``+{+( nameIR~field~ +:+ value~field~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``], for all ``id~t_field~`` in ``id~t_field~^{asterisk}^`` and ``value^?^`` in ``value^?^^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Check that ``value^?^`` is defined, for all ``value^?^`` in ``value^?^^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``value~field'~`` be ``value^?^``, for all ``value^?^`` in ``value^?^^{asterisk}^`` and ``value~field'~`` in ``value~field'~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let ``value~field_cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value~field'~`` casted to type ``typeIR~t_field~``], for all ``typeIR~t_field~`` in ``typeIR~t_field~^{asterisk}^``, ``value~field'~`` in ``value~field'~^{asterisk}^``, and ``value~field_cast~`` in ``value~field_cast~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Return ``+STRUCT+ typeId +{+( value~field_cast~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ typeId +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~t_field~ id~t_field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``+RECORD+ +{+( value~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``recordValue``.

 .. Let ``value^?^`` be xref:find_map[the value of ``id~t_field~`` in map ``+{+( nameIR~field~ +:+ value~field~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``], for all ``id~t_field~`` in ``id~t_field~^{asterisk}^`` and ``value^?^`` in ``value^?^^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Check that ``value^?^`` is defined, for all ``value^?^`` in ``value^?^^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``value~field'~`` be ``value^?^``, for all ``value^?^`` in ``value^?^^{asterisk}^`` and ``value~field'~`` in ``value~field'~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let ``value~field_cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value~field'~`` casted to type ``typeIR~t_field~``], for all ``typeIR~t_field~`` in ``typeIR~t_field~^{asterisk}^``, ``value~field'~`` in ``value~field'~^{asterisk}^``, and ``value~field_cast~`` in ``value~field_cast~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Return ``+HEADER+ typeId +{+true +;+ ( value~field_cast~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.

xref:cast_default[``defaultValue`` casted to type ``typeIR``]

. Return xref:default[the default value for type ``typeIR``].

xref:cast_invalid_header[``+{#}+`` casted to type ``typeIR``]

. If let ``headerTypeIR`` be ``typeIR``:
