xref:match_overloaded_named[Matching ``callTargetId +:+ V`` against named key ``nameIR~f~ +(+id~arg~^{asterisk}^+)+`` using parameter getter ``$get_parameterListIR``]

. Let ``nameIR +(+id~param~^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``callTargetId``.
. Check that ``nameIR`` is equal to ``nameIR~f~``.

. Let ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:get_parameterListIR[$get_parameterListIR(V)]``.
. Check that ``id~param~`` is equal to xref:id_of_parameterIR[the identifier of ``parameterIR``], for all ``id~param~`` in ``id~param~^{asterisk}^`` and ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``.

. Check that the length of ``id~param~^{asterisk}^`` is equal to the length of ``id~arg~^{asterisk}^``.

. Return xref:ite[``+MATCH+`` with defaults ``·`` and optionals ``·`` if ``+{+id~param~^{asterisk}^+}+`` is equal to ``+{+id~arg~^{asterisk}^+}+`` otherwise ``+NOMATCH+``].
. Let ``b~default~`` be xref:is_default_parameterIR[``parameterIR`` is a parameter with a default value], for all ``b~default~`` in ``b~default~^{asterisk}^`` and ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``.
. Let ``b~optional~`` be xref:is_optional_parameterIR[``parameterIR`` is an optional parameter], for all ``b~optional~`` in ``b~optional~^{asterisk}^`` and ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``.
. Check that the length of ``id~param~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than the length of ``id~arg~^{asterisk}^``.

. Let ``+{+id~param_omitted~^{asterisk}^+}+`` be xref:diff_set[the difference of the sets ``+{+id~param~^{asterisk}^+}+`` and ``+{+id~arg~^{asterisk}^+}+``].
. Let ``id~default_param~^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``id~param~^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``$is_default_parameterIR(parameterIR)^{asterisk}^``].
. Let ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``id~param_omitted~^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( id~param_omitted~ is in id~default_param~^{asterisk}^ )^{asterisk}^``].
. Let ``id~optional_param~^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``id~param~^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``$is_optional_parameterIR(parameterIR)^{asterisk}^``].
. Let ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``id~param_omitted~^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( id~param_omitted~ is in id~optional_param~^{asterisk}^ )^{asterisk}^``].
. Check that xref:eq_set[``+{+id~default~^{asterisk}^ {pp} id~optional~^{asterisk}^+}+`` is equal to ``+{+id~param_omitted~^{asterisk}^+}+``].

. Return xref:callTargetMatch[``+MATCH+`` with defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^``].

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``+NOMATCH+``.

xref:match_overloaded_unnamed[Matching ``callTargetId +:+ V`` against unnamed key ``nameIR~f~ +(+n~arg~+)+`` using parameter getter ``$get_parameterListIR``]

. Let ``nameIR +(+id~param~^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``callTargetId``.
. Check that ``nameIR`` is equal to ``nameIR~f~``.

. Let ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:get_parameterListIR[$get_parameterListIR(V)]``.
. Let ``b~default~`` be xref:is_default_parameterIR[``parameterIR`` is a parameter with a default value], for all ``b~default~`` in ``b~default~^{asterisk}^`` and ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``.
. Let ``b~optional~`` be xref:is_optional_parameterIR[``parameterIR`` is an optional parameter], for all ``b~optional~`` in ``b~optional~^{asterisk}^`` and ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``.
. Check that not xref:exists_[some of ``b~default~^{asterisk}^`` is true] and xref:exists_[some of ``b~optional~^{asterisk}^`` is true].

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that the length of ``id~param~^{asterisk}^`` is equal to ``n~arg~``.

  ... Return xref:callTargetMatch[``+MATCH+`` with defaults ``·`` and optionals ``·``].
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that the length of ``id~param~^{asterisk}^`` is greater than ``n~arg~``.

  ... Let ``( parameterIR~given~^{asterisk}^, parameterIR~omitted~^{asterisk}^ )`` be ``xref:partition_[$partition_<parameterIR>(parameterIR^{asterisk}^, n~arg~)]``.
  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that xref:is_optional_parameterIR[``parameterIR~omitted~`` is not an optional parameter], for all ``parameterIR~omitted~`` in ``parameterIR~omitted~^{asterisk}^``.

    ..... Check that xref:is_default_parameterIR[``parameterIR~omitted~`` is a parameter with a default value], for all ``parameterIR~omitted~`` in ``parameterIR~omitted~^{asterisk}^``.

    ..... Let ``id~default~`` be xref:id_of_parameterIR[the identifier of ``parameterIR~omitted~``], for all ``id~default~`` in ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and ``parameterIR~omitted~`` in ``parameterIR~omitted~^{asterisk}^``.
    ..... Return xref:callTargetMatch[``+MATCH+`` with defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``·``].
   .... {empty}
