  ... Let!~type~ ``nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR`` be ``argumentIR'``.

  ... Return xref:subexpressions_of_typedExpressionIR[the sub-expressions of ``typedExpressionIR``].

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``·``.

xref:subexpressions_of_argumentListIR[The sub-expressions of ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^``]

. Return ``xref:concat_[$concat_<typedExpressionIR>($subexpressions_of_argumentIR(argumentIR)^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:join_flow[The merged control flow of ``flow''`` and ``flow'''``]

. Check that ``flow''`` matches pattern ``+RET+``.

. Check that ``flow'''`` matches pattern ``+RET+``.

. Return ``+RET+``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``+CONT+``.

xref:empty_typeFrame[$empty_typeFrame]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_typeDefEnv[$empty_typeDefEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_callableTypeDefEnv[$empty_callableTypeDefEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_constructorTypeDefEnv[$empty_constructorTypeDefEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_typingContext[An empty typing context]

. Let ``globalTypingLayer`` be +{++CONSTRUCTOR+ ``xref:empty_constructorTypeDefEnv[$empty_constructorTypeDefEnv]``, +TYPE+ ``xref:empty_typeDefEnv[$empty_typeDefEnv]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableTypeDefEnv[$empty_callableTypeDefEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_typeFrame[$empty_typeFrame]``+}+.
. Let ``blockTypingLayer`` be +{++KIND+ ````, +TYPE+ ``xref:empty_typeDefEnv[$empty_typeDefEnv]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableTypeDefEnv[$empty_callableTypeDefEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_typeFrame[$empty_typeFrame]``+}+.
. Let ``localTypingLayer`` be +{++KIND+ ````, +TYPE+ ``xref:empty_typeDefEnv[$empty_typeDefEnv]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_typeFrame[$empty_typeFrame]``+}+.
. Let ``TC`` be +{++GLOBAL+ ``globalTypingLayer``, +BLOCK+ ``blockTypingLayer``, +LOCAL+ ``localTypingLayer``+}+.
. Return ``TC``.

xref:bound[Bound type variables from the ``cursor`` layer of ``TC``]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Return ``+{+·+}+``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Return xref:dom_map[the domain of the map ``TC.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+``].
. Else:
 .. Let ``B~block~`` be xref:bound[bound type variables from the ``+BLOCK+`` layer of ``TC``].
 .. Let ``B~local~`` be xref:dom_map[the domain of the map ``TC.+LOCAL+.+TYPE+``].
 .. Return xref:union_set[the union of the sets ``B~block~`` and ``B~local~``].

xref:enter_t[``TC`` with a new local frame]

. Return ``TC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``xref:empty_typeFrame[$empty_typeFrame] {two-colons} TC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.

