  ... Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
  ... Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+``.
. Else:
 .. If ``nameIR`` is equal to ``"verify"``:
  ... Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
  ... Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER_STATE+``.
 .. Else: return ``true``.

xref:callable_builtinMethod[$callable_builtinMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``true``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``true``.
. Else: return ``true``.

xref:callable_externMethod[$callable_externMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+``.
. Else: return ``true``.

xref:callable_externAbstractMethod[$callable_externAbstractMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+``.
. Else: return ``true``.

xref:callable_parserApplyMethod[$callable_parserApplyMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER_STATE+``.

xref:callable_controlApplyMethod[$callable_controlApplyMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+``.

xref:callable_tableApplyMethod[$callable_tableApplyMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+`` or ``localKind`` is equal to ``+TABLE_APPLY_METHOD+``.

xref:callableId_IR[The callable identifier for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``]

. Let ``++_++ ++_++ ++_++ id ++_++`` be ``parameterIR``, for all ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, ``id`` in ``id^{asterisk}^``, and ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``.
. Return ``nameIR +(+id^{asterisk}^+)+``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_callableDef[$parameterListIR_of_callableDef(callableDef)]

. If let ``actionDef`` be ``callableDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_actionDef[$parameterListIR_of_actionDef(actionDef)]``.
. Else if let ``functionDef`` be ``callableDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_functionDef[$parameterListIR_of_functionDef(functionDef)]``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_methodDef[$parameterListIR_of_methodDef(methodDef)]``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_actionDef[$parameterListIR_of_actionDef(annotationList +ACTION+ ++_++ +(+parameterListIR+)+ ++_++)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_functionDef[$parameterListIR_of_functionDef(functionDef)]

. If let ``definedFunctionDef`` be ``functionDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef(definedFunctionDef)]``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef(externFunctionDef)]``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef(+FUNCTION+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ ++_++)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef(+EXTERN_FUNCTION+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_methodDef[$parameterListIR_of_methodDef(methodDef)]

. If let ``externMethodDef`` be ``methodDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef(externMethodDef)]``.
. Else if let ``parserApplyMethodDef`` be ``methodDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef(parserApplyMethodDef)]``.
. Else if let ``controlApplyMethodDef`` be ``methodDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef(controlApplyMethodDef)]``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef(tableApplyMethodDef)]``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef(externMethodDef)]

. Let!~type~ ``+EXTERN_METHOD+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ ++_++^?^`` be ``externMethodDef``.

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef(+PARSER_APPLY+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ +;+ ++_+++}+)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef(+CONTROL_APPLY+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ +;+ ++_++ +;+ ++_+++}+)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef(+TABLE_APPLY+ +{+++_+++}+)]

. Return ``·``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_constructorDef[$parameterListIR_of_constructorDef(constructorDef)]

. If let ``+EXTERN+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+constructorParameterListIR+)+ +{+++_+++}+`` be ``constructorDef``:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.
. Else if let ``+PARSER+ +<+++_+++>+ +(+++_+++)+ +(+constructorParameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ ++_+++}+`` be ``constructorDef``:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.
. Else if let ``+CONTROL+ +<+++_+++>+ +(+++_+++)+ +(+constructorParameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ +APPLY+ ++_+++}+`` be ``constructorDef``:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.

xref:init_objectState[Initialization of ``nameIR````+<+`` ``typeIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+>+````+(+`` ``value^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+`` in the target]



xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_stateEnv[$empty_stateEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_constructorDefEnv[$empty_constructorDefEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_store[An empty store]

. Let ``store`` be xref:empty_map[an empty map].
. Return ``store``.

xref:add_store[``store`` where ``objectId`` to ``object`` is added]

. Let ``store'`` be xref:add_map[``store`` where ``objectId`` to ``object`` is added].
. Return ``store'``.

xref:find_store[The object ``objectId`` in ``store``]

. Let ``object`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``objectId`` in map ``store``].
. Return ``object``.

xref:empty_instContext[An empty instantiation context]

. Let ``globalInstLayer`` be +{++CONSTRUCTOR+ ``xref:empty_constructorDefEnv[$empty_constructorDefEnv]``, +TYPE+ ``xref:empty_typeDefEnv[$empty_typeDefEnv]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``blockInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]``, +STATE+ ``xref:empty_stateEnv[$empty_stateEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``localInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``IC`` be +{++PATH+ ``·``, +GLOBAL+ ``globalInstLayer``, +BLOCK+ ``blockInstLayer``, +LOCAL+ ``localInstLayer``+}+.
. Return ``IC``.

xref:enter_i[``IC`` with a new local frame]

. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame] {two-colons} IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.

xref:exit_i[``IC`` with the innermost frame removed]

. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:enter_path_i[``IC`` with ``id`` added to the path]

. Return ``IC`` with ``+PATH+`` set to ``IC.+PATH+ {pp} id``.

xref:inherit_i[An instantiation context same as ``IC`` up to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``blockInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]``, +STATE+ ``xref:empty_stateEnv[$empty_stateEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Let ``localInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Return ``IC[+BLOCK+ = blockInstLayer]`` with ``+LOCAL+`` set to ``localInstLayer``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``localInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+`` set to ``localInstLayer``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``IC``.

xref:add_var_i[``IC`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, value>(IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+))]``.

 .. Let ``frame`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, value>(IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+))]``.

 .. Let ``frame`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, value>(frame~h~))]``.

 .. Let ``frame~h'~`` be xref:add_map[``frame~h~`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~h'~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:add_vars_i[``IC`` where each of ``id^{asterisk}^`` to each of ``value^{asterisk}^`` are added to the ``p`` layer]

. If ``id^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``value^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``IC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``value~h~ {two-colons} value~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``value^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``IC'`` be xref:add_var_i[``IC`` where ``id~h~`` to ``value~h~`` is added to the ``p`` layer].
 .. Let ``IC''`` be xref:add_vars_i[``IC'`` where each of ``id~t~^{asterisk}^`` to each of ``value~t~^{asterisk}^`` are added to the ``p`` layer].
 .. Return ``IC''``.

xref:add_typeDef_i[``IC`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeDefIR`` is added to the ``cursor`` layer]

. Check that ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``.

. Let ``typeDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeDefIR`` is added].
. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+`` set to ``typeDefEnv``.

xref:add_parserState_i[``IC`` where ``nameIR`` to ``parserStateIR`` is added]

. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<nameIR>(nameIR, $dom_map<nameIR, parserStateIR>(IC.+BLOCK+.+STATE+))]``.

. Let ``stateEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+STATE+`` where ``nameIR`` to ``parserStateIR`` is added].
. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+STATE+`` set to ``stateEnv``.

xref:add_type_i[$add_type_i(cursor, IC, typeId, typeIR)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``theta`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeIR`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+TYPE+`` set to ``theta``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+LOCAL+``:
 .. Let ``theta`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+LOCAL+.+TYPE+`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeIR`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+TYPE+`` set to ``theta``.

xref:add_types_i[$add_types_i(p, IC, typeId^{asterisk}^, typeIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``typeId^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``typeIR^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``IC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``typeIR~h~ {two-colons} typeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``IC'`` be ``xref:add_type_i[$add_type_i(p, IC, typeId~h~, typeIR~h~)]``.
 .. Return ``xref:add_types_i[$add_types_i(p, IC', typeId~t~^{asterisk}^, typeIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.

