xref:add_callableDef_non_overload_i[``IC`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added as a non-overloaded callable to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``id +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``callableId``.
 .. Let ``+{+( id~k~ +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be xref:dom_map[the domain of the map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+``].
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, +{+id~k~^{asterisk}^+}+)]``.

 .. Let ``callableDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+`` set to ``callableDefEnv``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``id +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``callableId``.
 .. Let ``+{+( id~k~ +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be xref:dom_map[the domain of the map ``IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+``].
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, +{+id~k~^{asterisk}^+}+)]``.

 .. Let ``callableDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added].
