xref:find_var_i[The value of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p'`` layer of ``IC``]

. If let ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``].
 .. Return ``value``.
. Else:
 .. If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
  ... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``].
  ... Return ``value``.
 .. Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
  ... Let ``value'^?^`` be xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``].
  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Let!~type~ ``value`` be ``value'^?^``.

    ..... Return ``value``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``].

    ..... Return xref:find_var_i[the value of ``id`` from the ``+GLOBAL+`` layer of ``IC``].
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``value'^?^`` be xref:find_maps[the value of ``id`` in maps ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``].
  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Let!~type~ ``value`` be ``value'^?^``.

    ..... Return ``value``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:find_maps[the value of ``id`` in maps ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``].

    ..... Return xref:find_var_i[the value of ``id`` from the ``+BLOCK+`` layer of ``IC``].

xref:find_typeDef_i[The type definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``++_++`` layer of ``IC``]

. If let ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Return xref:find_map[the value of ``nameIR`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+``].
. Else:
 .. Return xref:find_map[the value of ``nameIR`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+``].

xref:find_constructorDef_i[The overloaded constructor definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+`` in ``IC``]

. If let ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Let ``callTargetKey`` be xref:callTargetKey[the call target key for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].
 .. Return xref:find_overloaded[finding the item in ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CONSTRUCTOR+`` matching ``callTargetKey`` using parameter getter ``$parameterListIR_of_constructorDef``].
. Else:
 .. Let ``callTargetKey`` be xref:callTargetKey[the call target key for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].
 .. Return xref:find_overloaded[finding the item in ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CONSTRUCTOR+`` matching ``callTargetKey`` using parameter getter ``$parameterListIR_of_constructorDef``].

xref:subst_type_i[``typeIR`` substituted by bound type variables in ``IC`` from the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Return ``typeIR``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``theta`` be ``IC.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+``.
 .. Let ``typeIR~subst~`` be xref:subst_typeIR[``typeIR`` substituted by ``theta``].
 .. Return ``typeIR~subst~``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``theta~block~`` be ``IC.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+``.
 .. Let ``theta~local~`` be ``IC.+LOCAL+.+TYPE+``.
 .. Let ``theta`` be ``xref:extend_map[$extend_map<typeId, typeIR>(theta~block~, theta~local~)]``.
 .. Let ``typeIR~subst~`` be xref:subst_typeIR[``typeIR`` substituted by ``theta``].
 .. Return ``typeIR~subst~``.

xref:Expr_inst[Expr_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of xref:typedExpressionIR[``expressionIR`` annotated with ``++_++``], under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``.

. If let ``booleanLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let ``boolValue`` be xref:ite[``true`` if ``booleanLiteral`` is equal to ``+TRUE+`` otherwise ``false``].
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``boolValue``.
. Else if let ``integerLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``integerLiteral``.
. Else if let ``stringLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``stringLiteral``.
. Else if let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let ``value`` be xref:find_var_i[the value of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p`` layer of ``IC``].
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``value``.
. Else if let ``defaultExpression`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Check that ``defaultExpression`` matches pattern ``+...+``.

 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``+DEFAULT+``.
. Else if let ``unop typedExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Result in store ``STO~1~`` and xref:un_op[``unop`` ``value``].
. Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~l~ binop typedExpressionIR~r~`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``binop`` is not in ``+[+ +&&+, +||+ +]+``.

   .... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~l~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
   .... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and xref:bin_op[``value~l~`` ``binop`` ``value~r~``].
  ... {empty}
   .... If ``binop`` matches pattern ``+&&+``:
    ..... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
    ..... Try:
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

      ....... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``false``.
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

      ....... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
      ....... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~``.
   .... Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+||+``:
    ..... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
    ..... Try:
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

      ....... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``true``.
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

      ....... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
      ....... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~``.
. Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~cond~ +?+ typedExpressionIR~true~ +:+ typedExpressionIR~false~`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~cond~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

   .... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~true~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~true~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~true~``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

   .... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~false~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~false~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~false~``.
. Else if let ``+(+typeIR+)+ typedExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``value~cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
 .. Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~cast~``.
. Else if let ``invalidHeaderExpression`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Check that ``invalidHeaderExpression`` matches pattern ``+{#}+``.

 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``+{#}+``.
. Else if let ``sequenceExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. If let ``+SEQ+ +{+typedExpressionListIR+}+`` be ``sequenceExpressionIR``:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionListIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionListIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^ +,+ +...++)+``.
. Else if let ``recordExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. If let ``+RECORD+ +{+( nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``recordExpressionIR``:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+RECORD+ +{+( value nameIR +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+RECORD+ +{+( value nameIR +;+ )^{asterisk}^ +,+ +...++}+``.
. Else if let ``+ERROR+ +.+ nameIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let ``nameIR~error~`` be ``"error."`` concatenated with ``nameIR``.
 .. Let ``value~error~`` be xref:find_var_i[the value of ``nameIR~error~`` from the ``p`` layer of ``IC``].
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``value~error~``.
. Else if let ``memberAccessBaseIR +.+ nameIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Let!~type~ ``+TYPE+ prefixedNameIR`` be ``memberAccessBaseIR``.

